      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:9a6537197490c7cafec176c78b5cbfe7cdacce217216b8b2afe7d72f0b7eff93",
      "text": "For external Case-event consumers, Streaming API and Pub/Sub differ in protocol, encoding, flow control, and CDC payload semantics. Streaming API uses CometD/Bayeux and JSON; Pub/Sub uses gRPC and Avro payloads with explicit demand. A migration must adapt decoding and field-change handling. Both APIs support replay within retention, so cursor persistence and deliberate restart choices matter with either API. Current Streaming API documentation also describes per-channel cursor updates starting with API version 68.0. Historical missed-event reports provide troubleshooting leads rather than proof of a universal protocol defect.",
